2.Draw a simple diagram (on paper or using any online tool) showing how a mobile app team is structured in a typical 
company, including at least: mobile developer, designer, backend/API developer, tester, and product manager.

                 ┌─────────────────────┐
                 │   PRODUCT MANAGER   │
                 │ Plans & coordinates │
                 └──────────┬──────────┘
                            │
          ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐
          │                 │                 │
          ▼                 ▼                 ▼
 ┌────────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌────────────────────┐
 │ MOBILE         │ │  DESIGNER    │ │ BACKEND / API      │
 │ DEVELOPER      │ │              │ │ DEVELOPER          │
 │                │ │ UI/UX Design │ │ Server & APIs      │
 │ Builds the app │ │              │ │ Database            │
 └───────┬────────┘ └──────┬───────┘ └──────────┬─────────┘
         │                 │                    │
         └─────────────────┼────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                  ┌─────────────────┐
                  │   TESTER / QA   │
                  │ Finds bugs &    │
                  │ tests the app   │
                  └────────┬────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                  ┌─────────────────┐
                  │   MOBILE APP    │
                  │  Final Product  │
                  └─────────────────┘

Short explanation:

Product Manager → plans the app and coordinates the team.
Designer → designs the UI/UX.
Mobile Developer → develops the Android/iOS app.
Backend/API Developer → handles server, database, and APIs.
Tester/QA → tests the app and finds bugs.
Mobile App → final product.
